.TH NOGFORGE 1 "October 2026" "nogForge v1.4.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
nogforge \- packages the KognogOS way: what is installed, installing, and updates, in a terminal
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nogforge
.br
.B nogforge \-\-version
.br
.B nogforge \-\-help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nogForge
is a keyboard-driven terminal application for the packages on KognogOS and
Arch Linux, built on
.BR nog (1),
the tier-aware package manager. Every package has a tier, and a new version
waits before it installs (30 days for the kernel and its kind, 15 for the
desktop, 7 for the rest).
.PP
nog decides; nogForge shows it. Tiers, holds, the day a hold ends and which
packages must move together come from nog
.RB ( "nog list \-\-json" ,
.BR "nog search \-\-json" ,
.BR "nog update \-\-json" )
and are never worked out a second time.
.PP
A change (install, remove, update, clean up) is reviewed first, then handed
to nog, which runs in a window inside nogForge (1.1): its steps and a
progress bar; nog's own screen opens when nog or pacman asks something,
when something fails, or on F12. pacman shows exactly what comes with a
change and asks before anything changes. The password is asked in
nogForge's own box
.RB ( "sudo \-A" ,
through a helper that asks the app), on a desktop and on a text console.
.PP
System packages are protected: Tier 1, Arch's
.B base
set and anything another package needs cannot be removed; the reason is
shown instead.
.PP
The full manual is inside the application (press
.BR F1 )
and in
.I /usr/lib/nogforge/nogforge/manual/
as Markdown.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.
.SH SCREENS
.TP
.B 1 \- Dashboard
Updates per source and tier, your packages per source and tier, the last
things nog did, and the space old downloads take.
.TP
.B 2 \- In-System
What is on this computer: badge, name, version, tier, repository, and an
Uninstall button (with Update beside it when nog has a newer version);
locked rows say why.
.TP
.B 3 \- Install
Search the repositories and the AUR, best matches first, and install.
.TP
.B 4 \- Update
nog's plan with your choices. Untick an update to keep it back (nog says
what must stay back with it); Promote makes a held one ready now. The ticked
ones are handed to nog by name
.RB ( "nog update a b c \-\-promote x" ),
so only they go in. Afterwards, What changed compares versions before and
after, and after a new kernel offers a restart.
.TP
.B 5 \- History
A menu of two screens: Activity (everything nog ran, in plain words) and
nog Logs (nog's own logs; Enter opens a run whole, as it appeared on screen).
.TP
.B 6 \- Help
A menu: the manual, every key, the license, About. Each shows as a page in
the main area; Esc goes back. A menu's number pressed again closes it.
.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B 1 \- 6
Go to a menu entry, left to right; History and Help open their menus.
.TP
.BR Ctrl +\fIletter\fR
The underlined letter of a menu entry: Ctrl+D, Ctrl+I, Ctrl+N, Ctrl+U,
Ctrl+S (History), Ctrl+H (Help). Works from inside a search box too. Each
letter is the first letter of the name, or the next free one when that is
taken; Help is always H, Quit Q.
.TP
.B u
Open Update; on Update, update the ticked ones.
.TP
.B k
Check for updates.
.TP
.B c
Clean up old downloads (asks first).
.TP
.B Space
Tick or untick an update.
.TP
.B Enter
The row's option: install, uninstall, promote; on nog Logs, open the run.
.TP
.BR / ,\  p
Search; the Repositories window.
.TP
.BR F1 ,\  ? ,\  q
Help on this screen; every key; quit (never while nog is working).
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nogforge/logs/YYYYMMDD nogforge-runs.csv
One line per session, written when nogForge closes.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/nog/logs/
nog's own logs, read by History.
.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
nog 1.7.0 or newer, python-forgekit 0.10.0 or newer (with python-pyte),
python-textual, python-rich. Optional: archlinux-appstream-data (app names
and badges).
.
